<title>CANADA: Low frost risk SE Manitoba, Alberta over weekend.</title>
<headline>Low frost risk SE Manitoba, Alberta over weekend.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A low risk of frost was forecast for southeastern Manitoba Saturday morning and a similar risk was seen on Alberta's west central and northwest grainbelt Sunday morning, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>A moderate risk was forecast for west central and northwest Alberta and a slight risk for the rest of the province was seen Sept 16 to 22, Environment Canada said in its 10-day frost outlook.</p>
<p>A slight risk of frost was forecast for eastern Saskatchewan and western Manitoba Sept 22.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
</text>
